         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Adding Around the World\n\nHumanity created many tools to count: bones, cords with knots, bars and dots, markers, beads and written numerals. Each people organized numbers in its own way, but all of them had to solve the same problem: **what happens when we reach ten?**\n\nIn this class we will use those same tools to add. In every tool we will look at how the group of ten becomes **1 carried to the next order**.\n\n#### What We Will Do\n\nFor each region of the world we will see a short explanation and then practice: add two numbers between 1 and 9 whose result is always 10 or more.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "a8f3c1d2-5b64-4e17-9c2a-1d0f3b6e8a02",
