            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "49bf2fba-e9f4-4650-ab96-4d4901795477",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=49bf2fba-e9f4-4650-ab96-4d4901795477",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Complement and the Carry\n\nBefore we use the tools, let us remember two ideas that make addition work.\n\nThe **complement to 10** of a digit is how much is still missing to reach ten. The complement of 9 is 1, the complement of 6 is 4, and the complement of 5 is 5.\n\nWhen the sum reaches ten, we group those ten units into one unit of the next order. That group is the **carry**, also called *advancing an order*. The digit that stays in the column is what is left outside the group of ten.\n\n**Example: 9 + 3.** The complement of 9 is 1. Because 3 is greater than or equal to 1, the ten can be completed: we take 1 from the 3, carry 1 to the next order, and 2 remain. Therefore, 9 + 3 = 12.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "a8f3c1d2-5b64-4e17-9c2a-1d0f3b6e8a03",
