         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### In Africa: Adding with Bones\n\nThe first counting marks we know of were made on bones. To add, people did not need a new tool: they simply kept marking. Thousands of years ago people did not yet use the carry. They made continuous marks in a row along the bone: to add 9 + 3, they made 12 marks, one after another, instead of turning ten marks into a ten of the next order.\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and place on the bone the total number of marks. Count one mark for each unit of the result.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
