            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "49bf2fba-e9f4-4650-ab96-4d4901795477",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=49bf2fba-e9f4-4650-ab96-4d4901795477",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### In America: Adding with Quipus\n\nThe quipu records numbers with knots on a hanging cord: the units are at the bottom and the tens are stacked above. A knot in the units order is worth 1; when that order reaches ten knots, those ten are removed and one knot is placed in the tens order above. The result appears as one knot in the tens order and the remaining knots in the units order.\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers. Place knots in the **Units** order at the bottom of the cord; when that order reaches ten knots, the game removes them and adds one knot to the **Tens** order above.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "a8f3c1d2-5b64-4e17-9c2a-1d0f3b6e8a06",
