            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "49bf2fba-e9f4-4650-ab96-4d4901795477",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=49bf2fba-e9f4-4650-ab96-4d4901795477",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### In America: Adding with Mesoamerican Numbers\n\nIn the Mesoamerican system a dot is worth 1 and a bar is worth 5. To add, write the result with bars and dots: the bars are always horizontal and the dots sit above them. Two bars are worth 10.\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and represent the result with dots and bars. For example, 9 + 3 = 12 is written with two horizontal bars and two dots above them.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
