         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### In America: Adding with the Yupana\n\nThe yupana, used together with the quipus, places seeds on a grid where each row is a place value. In this class we use the *Tawa Pukllay* method: the first number is marked in one color, the second in another, and the result in green; when a row reaches ten, one marker moves to the row above.\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers with the yupana. Mark the units row until it reaches ten; then the ten becomes one marker in the tens row above.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
